Hope this isn't in the FAQ or something, but here goes.  (This is all
on the DOS version.)

I guess these might be spoilers, but minor if so:


I was playing a chaotic elf, and got to the town level of the Gnomish
Mines.  Just my luck, the priestess was not chaotic.  I was pretty tough,
so I put on a blindfold and killed her.  I eventually got the altar 
converted (with a white unicorn >8-).  I hadn't yet checked out the
shops, and when I did, all the shopkeepers ignored me!  It said that
the shop seemed deserted.  Also, every time I entered the temple room,
I got a message such as "You have an eerie feeling" or "You feel you
are being watched."  About every third time, I was attacked by a ghost.

Now for the worst.  With no warning, the game crashed with a segmentation
error.  (Luckily I had my save file copied away...not for cheating of 
course, but just in case this happened. ;)  Alas, when I restarted, the
game crashed every time I tried to enter a shop (even if I just tried
to zap the wall with a wand of digging.)  And it is a pretty nasty crash
since it leaves DOS messed up so that dir/w produces trashy output!
The only thing I thought might be causing the crash was that I was low
on disk space, and might have run out.  It still keeps crashing even
with more space, but now my save file is corrupted, I guess.

Two questions.  Any idea what the crash is about?  And did my killing
the priestess make the shopkeepers weird out on me?

Oh, one more slightly amusing thing.  I had sacrificed an elf or something
and summoned Yeenoghu, so he was wandering around the level.  A little later
I was given Stormbringer.  A touchy combination...one false move, and you
have a pissed off demon prince!
